WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.270
Dr. Alexei, more commonly known as just Alexei,
was likely born in the late 1940s, and raised

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.700
in Soviet Russia, where he went on to become
a scientist, where he would develop a machine

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.290
designed to open a gate into the alternate
realm known as the Upside Down.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.610
This is the same thing that Dr. Martin Brenner
was trying to utilize Eleven and MK-Ultra

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.840
for two years earlier.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.940
However, when Alexei is abducted by Jim Hopper
and Joyce Byers, he proves to be more than

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.420
just a Russian scientist.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:29.590
Alexei is an individual with his own dreams
and ambitions to become... a consumer of slurpees

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.190
and Burger King?

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:40.600
“Two Whoppers, extra ketchup, large fry, and one
extra large, slurpee.”

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.540
Alexei is actually not alone in his excitement
over commodities from the United States, 

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.700
they play a direct role in what leads to his
eventual death.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.480
And no, I don’t mean from the sugars, fats
and cholesterol of the food Alexei likes to

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.018
eat.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:56.010
To learn more about Alexei and why his love
of cherry slurpees is actually very important,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.859
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.350
Welcome to Horror History -- in this lesson
I’ll be covering the life and meaning of

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.729
this Looney Tune loving commie from the third
season of Stranger Things.

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:12.100
The funny thing is, Alexei’s story kind
of comes true in a way for the actor that

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.549
played him, Alec Utgoff.

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:17.039
He really did grow up in Soviet Russia and
although it looks like he now resides in the

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:21.009
UK, he is kind of living the American dream,
or at least some version of it, by starring

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:24.649
in massive American productions like Jack
Ryan and Stranger Things.

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:27.829
To fully understand Alexei, I’m going to
look back at everything he's experienced

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:31.439
over the course of his life, his excitement
over consumerism, and why his death is more

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:32.925
significant than you might think.

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:41.950
As I mentioned, it looks like Alexei is born
in the late 1940s, just judging off of his

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.450
appearance.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.130
This would be just shortly after World War
II, and at this time, Joseph Stalin put, what

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.560
was referred to by Winston Churchill as the
“iron curtain” in place.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.770
This essentially cut off the Soviet Union
from any contact with non-communist countries,

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.789
which included getting any kind of imports,
including food, music, toys, and, yes, even

00:01:58.789 --> 00:01:59.789
slurpees.

00:01:59.789 --> 00:02:03.020
As Winston Churchhill put it, in his 1946
speech at Westminster College in Missouri,

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:09.020
“From Stettin in the Baltic to Trieste in
the Adriatic, an iron curtain has descended

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.450
across the continent.”

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.430
This means that Alexei would have grown up
with a very strict life under constant surveillance,

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.790
and commodities of more western cultures,
especially the United States, would have been

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.900
things that he could only have access to from
the black market.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.140
And if he were caught enjoying these things,
there would be severe consequences.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.079
The theme of the comparison of consumer capitalism
mapped over the falling of the Soviet Union,

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:30.060
is abundant in season three of Stranger Things.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.760
It starts with a commentary by Erica Sinclair,
(of all people) the younger sister of Lucas.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.859
Even though she’s just a kid, she frequently
mentions her love of capitalism.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:41.030
"Do you know what I love most about this country?

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.030
Capitalism"

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.620
...and her dislike of communism.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.920
“Just because I don't agree with communism as
an ideology..."

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.750
This is also signified later in the season
where Steve Harrington is being brutally interrogated

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.980
by Comrade General Stepanov, and tries to
get out of it by offering him a “Scoops

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:58.385
Ahoy” flavor, the “S.S. Butterscotch”
to which Stepanov laughs in Steve’s face.

00:03:00.757 --> 00:03:04.280
Or again later, when Hopper and Murray try
to pass as Soviet soldiers, by Murray making

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.586
a joke about secretly drinking vodka, while
also identifying that individualism is something

00:03:08.586 --> 00:03:09.567
to be shamed.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.567
"Say goodbye to sunlight."
«Попрощайтесь с солнечным светом».

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:15.288
"Who needs sunlight when we have one another, comrade?"
"Кому нужен солнечный свет, когда мы друг с другом, товарищ?"

00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:17.216
"Indeed comrade."
"Действительно товарищ".

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:18.899
"And a bottle of Stolichnaya."
«И бутылку Столичной».

00:03:18.899 --> 00:03:21.185
*laughs in Russian*

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:27.709
Alexei is first introduced in 1984, as a Russian
scientist, working on a giant drill in an

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:28.829
underground bunker.

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:32.540
When the drill backfires and eviscerates everyone
in it’s proximity, Alexei witnesses the

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.140
very “Darth Vader like” murder of his
direct supervisor at the hands of the dead

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.530
eye-ed henchman, Grigori, at the request of
Comrade General Stepanov.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.580
As Alexei watches this punishment unfold,
he is informed that we will have

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.950
one year to fix the problems and make
the machine work, assuming that if he doesn’t,

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.310
he will meet a similar fate to his predecessor.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.920
Alexei is seen again, one year later, in July
of 1985, when Dustin sets up his radio in

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.040
an attempt to connect with his summer girlfriend,
only to accidentally intercept a Russian transmission

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.040
that he can’t understand.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.620
The transmission is actually a code that’s
coming from the same underground bunker as

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.569
earlier, only now Alexei and his team have
made some progress.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.175
“Beautiful isn’t it?”
"Красиво, не правда ли?"

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:13.990
Dustin gets very concerned with intercepting
this message, which is a reflection on the

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:17.780
fear throughout the U.S. of communism, as
mentioned in an earlier episode of Horror

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.470
History on the Demogorgon.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:23.350
In season three, however, the threat of communism
and the Cold War is much more blatant.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:26.650
Even though he’s a kid, it makes sense that
Dustin would be aware of the danger posed

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:30.750
by the Russians, cause it was evident in the
movies that were released in 1985, when this storyline

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.750
takes place.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.940
It can be assumed that Alexei continued to
work on the machine as if his life depended

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.870
on it, but he is not seen again until he,
for some reason, is in an underground bunker

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.770
of the Hess Family Farm with… this guy.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.380
That’s when Joyce Byers and Jim Hopper break
in, they confront Alexei at gunpoint, where

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.940
it is made clear that Alexei does not speak
English:

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.330
Alexei: (Russian)
Jim: “I can’t understand you!”

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.280
Alexei finds himself in the middle of a scary
combat situation between Hopper and Grigori

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.400
-- that scary dead eyed henchmen who killed
his predecessor -- a battle which ends in

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.050
Alexei being abducted by Joyce and Hopper.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.630
“You’re coming with us!”

00:05:11.893 --> 00:05:16.680
Up until now, Alexei hasn’t had much opportunity
to show any individual personality, and how

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:17.180
could he?

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.770
He’s had one job to do, which is to make
a drill work, and his comrade general expects

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.590
him to do pretty much only that.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.870
Now that he is captured by Joyce and Hopper,
initially there is still not a ton of room

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:29.740
for his individual personality to show, apart
from him expressing that he may know a better

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:34.132
way to fix Hopper’s car when it breaks down,
only to be ignored, as the car explodes.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.630
That is, until Joyce and Hopper get into an
argument in the woods, stop paying attention

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.530
and Alexei is able to make a run for it, and
escape from them.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.210
It seems like Alexei might have a shot at
getting away until he comes to an abrupt stop

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.560
on his own, pointing and smiling at something.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.220
As Hopper catches up to him, what he is smiling
at is revealed.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.460
It’s a 7-Eleven.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:58.150
Alexei wears an expression that looks like
a child who’s about to enter Disneyland.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:02.330
Alexei, Joyce and Hopper all pound back coca-cola,
which by the way is not a great choice to

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.319
hydrate, especially if you’ve been running
through the woods.

00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:05.319
Without water.

00:06:05.319 --> 00:06:08.470
But it is one of many examples in season three
of Stranger Things where product placement

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.900
is heavily showcased.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.020
Similar to the Eggo Waffles from the previous
two seasons, the product placement in season

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.900
three is deliberate and holds significant
meaning, especially for Alexei.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.259
As I mentioned earlier, the rise of American
consumerism of the 1980s is all over Stranger

00:06:21.259 --> 00:06:24.090
Things season three, with the introduction
of the new Starcourt mall.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.720
The mall is a pretty direct symbol of the
shifting of the American Dream and the end

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.720
of the Cold War.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.930
Hawkins’ small town values are being directly
threatened and altered, by showing small businesses

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.129
closing, as everyone clambors to the new mall.

00:06:35.129 --> 00:06:36.520
Even Hopper’s wardrobe changes.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:41.120
Stranger Things is known for its nostalgia
for movies of the early 1980s, but the Starcourt

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.210
mall allows for a new type of 80s nostalgia.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.830
This is towards the fashion styles, music
and products from this time period.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.270
This even includes a light hearted shopping
montage with Eleven and Max to Madonna’s

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:53.129
"Material Girl", similar to some commercials
of that era.

00:06:53.129 --> 00:06:57.370
As always, the show pays a very accurate tribute
to logos and ad campaigns from this time.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.880
Even going so far as to include the big fail
that was “New Coke” by having Lucas try

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.220
to compare New Coke to John Carpenter’s
The Thing.

00:07:03.364 --> 00:07:05.125
LUCAS: “It’s like Carpenter’s The Thing.

00:07:05.125 --> 00:07:06.973
The original… is a classic.

00:07:06.973 --> 00:07:08.410
No question about it.

00:07:08.883 --> 00:07:09.883
But the remake…

00:07:10.052 --> 00:07:11.604
*sips Cola*

00:07:11.729 --> 00:07:12.729
Sweeter.

00:07:13.168 --> 00:07:14.168
Bolder.

00:07:14.879 --> 00:07:15.928
Better.”

00:07:16.177 --> 00:07:17.201
MIKE: “You’re insane.”

00:07:17.201 --> 00:07:20.830
I wasn’t around for New Coke, but The Thing…
pretty good.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.060
But what does any of this have to do with
Alexei?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:27.010
It is revealed that the Starcourt Mall is
actually a front for the secret Russian operation

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:28.580
several miles beneath the mall.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:33.849
Hopper and Joyce commandeer a Cadillac Eldorado
convertible from a very... 1980s... guy.

00:07:33.849 --> 00:07:37.640
Then they bring Alexei to the only person
they know who speaks Russian who, naturally, is

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.567
Murray Bauman.

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:43.139
Now having a translator, English speaking
audiences such as myself and 99% of you get

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:45.740
to experience Alexei’s personality for the
first time.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:50.330
We learn that Alexei loves Looney Tunes, Burger
King and is passionate about cherry slurpees.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.330
Roll the clip.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.056
“Tell that stupid man it is not the same
in the slightest.
«Скажи этому глупому человеку, что это не то же самое.
ни в малейшей степени.

00:07:54.056 --> 00:07:56.826
And I would like the Cherry I requested.”
И я бы хотел вишню, которую просил ».

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.889
“He respectfully disagrees.”

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:01.650
Shortly after this, Alexei is released with
the keys to the convertible.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:06.129
He is visibly thrilled at the idea of taking
this luxury American vehicle for a joyride.

00:08:06.129 --> 00:08:09.099
He gets behind the wheel, floors it and just
when it seems like he’s going to leave his

00:08:09.099 --> 00:08:13.560
captors behind, he makes the surprising choice
to stop, turn around and go back to join them.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.259
He even concedes that a strawberry slurpee
tastes the same as cherry.

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:20.900
They make a pitstop Hawkins’s 4th of July
Carnival, and it is here that Alexei reveals

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.120
to Murray how badly he wants to enjoy western
commodities, by asking:

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.977
Alexei: “And I become an American citizen
and join the fun, yes?”
"И я стал гражданином Америки.
и присоединяйся к веселью, да? "

00:08:30.397 --> 00:08:34.380
Murray “Who said you had to be an American
to join the fun?”
«Кто сказал, что ты должен быть американцем?
присоединиться к веселью? "

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.720
Murray very directly addresses what the American
Dream would appear to be to Alexei by saying

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:44.200
“It doesn’t get any more American than
this my friend.
«Нет ничего более американского, чем
это мой друг.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.480
Fatty foods, ugly decadency… rigged games…”
Жирная пища, уродливое упадок сил… сфальсифицированные игры… »

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.720
Alexei’s whole demeanor is often almost
childlike.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:53.540
He loves sweets and asks repeatedly if he
can watch Looney Tunes.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.860
Even when he plays darts at the carnival,
he is surrounded by children who cheer for

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:58.120
him, as if he is just another child.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.920
This actually makes a lot of sense when you
consider Alexei’s background and what many

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.650
Russian citizens were experiencing during
this time period.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:08.651
In 1985, the year that Stranger Things season
three takes place, Mikhail Gorbachev 

00:09:08.651 --> 00:09:12.130
had come to power in Soviet
Russia with the goal to democratize the U.S.S.R.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:16.810
Where Stalin had put up an Iron Curtain,
Gorbachev promoted new policies of glasnost

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.720
and perestroika, or openness
and restructuring.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.160
Ronald Reagan and Gorbachev signed a culture
agreement through Geneva in order to open

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.820
communication with the west.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:28.290
And it’s thanks to this, that we now have
the internet video of Billy Joel having a

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.300
mental breakdown on stage.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:33.262
What does Billy Joel flipping over his piano
while his band continues to rock out 

00:09:33.262 --> 00:09:34.410
have to do with Alexei?

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:39.090
This Billy Joel performance was part of a
huge tour across the U.S.S.R in 1987.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:43.730
This tour was a very big deal in opening communication
between the United States and Soviet countries.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:47.730
While other singers and rock stars had performed
in small venues in the U.S.S.R, Billy Joel

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.590
was the first to do a large amphitheatre size
rock show, and naturally, there was a lot

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:52.590
of pressure on him.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.510
As Billy Joel performs, he can be heard yelling
at his camera crew “stop lighting the audience.”

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:00.150
What was happening was there were filmmakers
working on a documentary about the tour.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:03.200
They wanted to get footage of the Russian
audience enjoying the show but, every time

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.580
the lights would come up on the crowd, the
audience would completely freeze.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.601
This was because they, like Alexei, had grown
up under strict communist surveillance, where

00:10:10.601 --> 00:10:13.830
enjoying western culture, was illegal and
considered a betrayal.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:17.160
There may have been new leadership in place,
but openly enjoying something like this was

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.500
still kind of taboo.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:22.600
So Alexei openly enjoying Looney Tunes, Burger
King, slurpees, and carnival games, would

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.990
be something he likely wouldn’t be comfortable
doing in front of his Russian superiors.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:30.700
Especially considering that the guy in charge
wasn’t exactly all about fun and games.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:34.870
So, when Alexei wins the carnival dart game,
and shows off his giant Woody Woodpecker prize

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:39.280
with a huge smile on his face, it means so
much more to him than what we see on the surface.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:43.360
Alexei, like many other Russians, missed out
on consumerism as a child and is now making

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.560
up for lost time.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:48.030
Which makes it all the more crushing when
he sees Grigori appear.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.820
When Grigori whispers “traitor” to Alexei
as he passes him after shooting him in the

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:55.150
chest, this isn’t just because Alexei was
helping Hopper, Joyce and Murray in stopping

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:59.100
the Russians from opening the Upside Down,
but also because Alexei’s enjoyment of American

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.370
culture was seen as a direct betrayal of his
Soviet regime.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:06.130
Maybe it’s because of this, that Alexei’s
death, even though he’s just more of a secondary

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.010
protagonist, hurts so much.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.290
Or maybe it’s because of his new best friendship
with Murray.

00:11:11.015 --> 00:11:11.790
“Murray!

00:11:13.274 --> 00:11:14.500
Look!
Смотри!

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.986
It’s not rigged!”
Это не подстроено! "

00:11:16.111 --> 00:11:16.873
“Ah!”

00:11:16.873 --> 00:11:18.636
*Laughs like Woody the Woodpecker*

00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:22.700
Either way, watching Alexei die is one of
the many tragic losses that takes place in

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.180
Stranger Things season three.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.180
“I..

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:27.210
I just left for a minute for a corn dog.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.120
A stupid corn dog!”

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.700
Don’t leave for a corn dog.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.550
Stay here and check out another episode of
Horror History.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:36.430
Just click that video on the left, and let
me know what other Stranger Things characters

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:37.510
you’d like to see me cover.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:41.440
Make sure you show your love of American culture
by subscribing to CZsWorld for new horrors

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:46.880
every week, ring that deathbell for all notifications
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.550
Assuming we both survive.

